WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.186
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.186 --> 00:00:04.519
(drum roll)

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.293
- All right.

00:00:06.293 --> 00:00:07.126
So they given me extra.

00:00:07.126 --> 00:00:09.543
'cause we love Charles
actually extra. Yeah.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.150
I didn't know this about
you, but you start,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.770
and I feel like I've known you for a bit,

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.583
but like you started
on Broadway. I didn't.

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:17.600
- I started on Broadway.
I didn't finish it.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.650
- I know, but I didn't know that.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.557
- Well. Yeah. Well, I mean, I love

00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:22.969
that you, New York suits you.

00:00:22.969 --> 00:00:24.318
- I love New York.

00:00:24.318 --> 00:00:25.151
- Really well. I can tell that Kelly.

00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:25.984
It comes right through the screen.

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:26.866
- Yeah.

00:00:26.866 --> 00:00:28.140
- And it suited me for a quick minute.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.610
I was in Los Angeles and auditioned

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.920
for the show called Smokey Joe's Cafe.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.930
It was a review of the songs of Lieber

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.220
and Stoller's. So great.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.870
- I perform that pop choir in high school.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.703
- You did?

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:38.536
- Yep.

00:00:38.536 --> 00:00:40.110
- Years before that I
auditioned for the Broadway show

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.720
and I just had a really great audition.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.000
For years before that, I
would get a vocal audition

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.930
for a Broadway show

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.505
and they'd go, all right,
they wanna see a callback.

00:00:47.505 --> 00:00:49.440
And I go, for what?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.780
And they say, oh, they,
it's a dance audition.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.160
I go, well I don't dance,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.290
so I probably shouldn't go do that.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.257
- Yeah. Just show up
and lie and say you can.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.680
- No, That's what they said.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.030
They just wanna see if you can move.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.560
And apparently I can't move.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.770
But anyway, this one audition,
I just was free and loose.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.360
I did a couple Elvis songs. Hound dog.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.265
Leiber and Stoller wrote
Hound Dog and Jailhouse Rock.

00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:09.098
- Yeah.

00:01:09.098 --> 00:01:10.620
- And so I think I bamboozled them.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.480
And then I went here and Broadway

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.730
and we were rehearsing
in the studios downtown.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.860
And I looked around and I
was surrounded by people

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.380
that were just legit Broadway talent.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.585
My leading lady was DeLee
Lively and she was unbelievable.

00:01:21.585 --> 00:01:23.292
Such a great dancer, singer.

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:26.340
And then I think it was
about three weeks in,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.010
the director finally showed
up to see where we were.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.923
And I could just see on
his face him watching me,

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.250
you know that thing we have
like imposter syndrome?

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.050
And you're like, I don't belong here

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.277
and everybody's gonna figure that out.

00:01:39.277 --> 00:01:40.950
- Yeah. I have that all the time.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.540
- Well, they figured it out.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.000
I'll tell you. He looked
at me and he said in

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.861
front of everybody, he
stopped the whole thing.

00:01:46.861 --> 00:01:50.100
He goes, let me ask you
a question. Do you dance?

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.180
And I said, well Jerry,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.470
that falls under things you

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.170
should have asked at the audition.

00:01:56.063 --> 00:01:57.870
And I said, I'm doing my best.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.985
I will get it by Showtime.
I promise you that.

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:03.090
About a week later he gave
me a very nice phone call

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.710
and he said, we really
appreciate your hard work,

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.373
but we're gonna have to.

00:02:06.373 --> 00:02:07.206
- Oh.

00:02:07.206 --> 00:02:08.039
- So they recast the role.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:08.872
- Oh, man.

00:02:09.974 --> 00:02:11.400
- And the first thing I found
out was that I had a contract.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.223
So I got paid for a year
for not being in that show.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.323
- That's amazing.

00:02:16.323 --> 00:02:17.820
- That's like the one time
you're thankful for contracts.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.260
- It was unbelievable.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.300
I met six months in, I go to my mailbox,

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.470
I'm like, honey, I got a raise.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.730
I got a bump at six months.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:24.930
So, and another thing

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.910
I found out is if I had done that show,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.202
I would not have been available to get on

00:02:28.202 --> 00:02:30.030
Whose Line Is it Anyway?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:30.863
- Oh, love.

00:02:30.863 --> 00:02:31.740
- Which changed my life being on

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.420
that show for a number of years.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.910
And then a final couple, two things.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.740
Years later, six or eight years later,

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.770
we're walking some fair in in
L.A. and we see DeLee Lively

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.805
and her husband, who was the
guy they replaced me with.

00:02:45.805 --> 00:02:46.890
- Oh.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.330
- All these things had to happen.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.520
- They had three kids,
they had one in her arm,

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.980
one in the stroller, one
walking, and they were amazing.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.390
And we talked and it was really even I go,

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.700
I think it's very important
that you guys understand

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.890
and know and remember that
you have all this bliss.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.450
You have this paradise

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.818
because Charles Esten can't dance.

00:03:02.818 --> 00:03:04.721
(guests laughing)

00:03:04.721 --> 00:03:06.221
- You are welcome.

